</div><p class="start"><strong>Where to start.</strong> Compare your PEPY with the middle half for your company type, not the overall spread.</p><div class="deep-accordion"><details><summary><div class="acc-summary-inner"><div class="acc-summary-label">In full</div><div class="acc-summary-title">Startups, MNCs and size: the detail</div><div class="acc-summary-sub">1 min read</div></div><span class="deep-acc-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="deep-acc-body"><p>Spend per employee rises with company size here, even though insurers charge larger groups less for the same policy. The reason is design: larger companies are far more likely to cover parents, about 6 in 10 of those with 200+ employees against fewer than 3 in 10 small businesses.</p><details class="as-table"><summary>See all groups as a table</summary>
